From 3a9fe5c35943dfcc2328b92ba3184709e9178b6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dane Brouwer <27723770+Danebrouwer97@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:45:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Live audio and push-to-talk for camera streams

/audio/<sn> serves a camera's live audio (AAC-LC as ADTS, A-law as WAV) from a
live() consumer on the shared source. go2rtc lists it as a second source of
each camera stream, converted to Opus, so WebRTC viewers hear the camera. It
only rides on an open /stream and stops with the last one, so it never wakes
a camera or keeps one awake.

/talk/<sn> takes a streamed POST of PCM (s16le 16 kHz or A-law 8 kHz),
encodes it to AAC-LC with ffmpeg and plays it through the camera's talkback.
It needs a live view, and only answers BRIDGE_TALK_ALLOW (default: loopback
and the Supervisor network), since the bridge's HTTP has no auth.

BRIDGE_LIVE_AUDIO=0 restores the single video source.
